; Regression (2026-09-20): a frame-local reference that leaves through a
; CALLEE'S CONSTRUCTION. The escape checker refused a frame-local reference
; that is returned or stored by a plain `set`, and said nothing when it
; travelled into a callee that puts it inside a new object on a NAMED region —
; in ../tscaly/packages/tscaly 174 frame-local lists reached
; `box_node_data[T](host, T(... list ...))` and compiled clean; the program
; died of an unbounded recursion that the whole gate chain missed.
;
; The callee is marked in the escape summary now (a reference parameter that
; is a component of a `T^name(...)` construction), and the existing call-site
; check does the rest. `escape_via_construction_ok.scaly` is the control: the
; same callee with a page-hosted argument stays legal.
; xfail: error: reference into a local page escapes via call

define Leaf (n: int)
define Keeper (items: ref[Array[ref[Leaf]?]])

procedure box_it(host: ref[Page], items: ref[Array[ref[Leaf]?]]) returns ref[Keeper]
    &Keeper^host(items)

procedure build(host: ref[Page]) returns ref[Keeper]
{
    let list &Array[ref[Leaf]?]()
    box_it(host, list)
}
